.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-REPLAY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-replay - Deliberately replay one retained HTTP request to the same origin


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel replay <tunnel> <capture-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Deliberately replay one retained HTTP request to the same origin

.PP
Replay one retained HTTP request to the same tunnel origin and route. This can repeat a side effect; use the capture identity and optional idempotency key deliberately.

.PP
Durable tunnels retain identity, routes, connectors, and domains across client sessions. Ephemeral tunnels have a separate lifecycle. Route publication and browser HTTP access require exact authorization; TLS for browser HTTP terminates at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for replay

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	explicit idempotency key for safe retry (generated when omitted)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--route\fP=""
	replay a capture from one route ID (required when the tunnel has several routes)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
